diff --git a/CHANGELOG.md b/CHANGELOG.md
index b2eea38..7f5ee85 100644
--- a/CHANGELOG.md
+++ b/CHANGELOG.md
@@ -2,8 +2,14 @@
 
 ## Unreleased
 
+- Physical Hermes 2.16-inch overlay: hold +/KEY for a touch/button session browser; list this device's recent history and resume through Hermes on the host. PWR can sleep the idle browser.
+
 ### Hardware and setup
 
+- AMOLED-2.16: enable the physical +/KEY (GPIO18) as CANCEL; a single click cancels and a double-click starts a fresh Hermes session. Double-click behavior is opt-in per board and excludes touch gestures, settings and approval prompts.
+
+- AMOLED-2.16: keep header labels and footer hints clear of the rounded visible screen corners with 48-pixel side insets. The framebuffer and central content stay 480×480. Footer text now respects a rectangular panel's existing corner inset.
+
 - Board support for the Waveshare ESP32-S3-Knob-Touch-LCD-1.8: round 360×360 SH8601 QSPI LCD (Espressif's `esp_lcd_sh8601`), CST816S touch, one PDM microphone, a rotary encoder that scrolls, ESP32-S3R8 with 16 MB flash and 8 MB PSRAM. Hold the screen or BOOT to talk. The port doesn't drive the board's headphone DAC, so replies are shown as text and not played. The panel's initialization table comes from Waveshare's ESP-IDF demo. Adds a `sim-360x360-knob` simulator profile. Experimental: a contributor test showed the display, hold-to-talk touch and microphone capture through a full voice turn; the full checklist is not completed. Contributed by @Delphus123.
 - With `latch_power.usb_external_power`, the latch power driver reports external power while the charging signal is on or a USB host is connected to the S3's own USB port. Boards with a battery latch and no USB-status input could not tell battery from USB, so Wi-Fi modem sleep never applied on battery. The Spotpear muma now reports its battery voltage (divider by two on GPIO 1) and charging signal (GPIO 41), and both the muma and the Waveshare LCD-1.54 report external power. Contributed by Luiz Gustavo Saraiva (@luizgustavosaraiva).
 - Board support for Espressif's ESP-VoCat, v1.2 only: round 360×360 ST77916 QSPI panel, CST816S touch, ES7210 microphones, ES8311 speaker output through an NS4150B amplifier, 16 MB flash and 16 MB PSRAM. BOOT talks as well as the screen. The panel takes Espressif's own start-up table from the ESP-VoCat BSP, so ST77916 boards can now choose their table (`lcd.st77916_panel`) instead of having it picked by the Waveshare panel ID, and boards can switch GPIO-driven supplies on at boot (`power_rails`), which the VoCat needs for its LCD/SD rail and codec supply. The BMI270 IMU, BQ27220 fuel gauge, head touch pads and LED are not used yet. Experimental: a contributor smoke test on USB power covered boot, display, both codecs, touch, Wi-Fi, pairing and a hold-to-talk voice turn; the full checklist is not completed. Contributed by @dreamhunter02.
diff --git a/docs/protocol.md b/docs/protocol.md
index 2c5d078..dd6455c 100644
--- a/docs/protocol.md
+++ b/docs/protocol.md
@@ -285,3 +285,19 @@ Boards whose firmware enables Bluetooth (none yet; see [hardware validation](har
 - `proto` is a single integer, and a server rejects versions it does not speak.
 - Adding optional fields or new message types does not change the version. Receivers ignore unknown types and fields.
 - Changing the meaning of an existing field does.
+
+
+## Physical Hermes session browser extension
+
+Paired 2.16-inch devices may request `{"type":"session.list","id":"s1"}`.
+The matching plugin replies with the same type/id and `sessions`, containing up to
+20 `{id,title,detail,current}` rows scoped to the device/profile. `detail` is a
+human-readable activity date; errors include `error` and an empty list.
+
+`{"type":"session.select","id":"s2","session":"EXACT_LISTED_ID"}` requests a
+switch through Hermes `/resume`. Only recently listed IDs are accepted; normal
+Hermes ownership and active-turn rules still apply. The correlated reply is
+`{"type":"session.selected","id":"s2","ok":true}` or `ok:false,error:"..."`.
+The device ignores stale replies and times out after 10 seconds. Opening or
+closing the browser sends no conversation reset. Firmware and Mac plugin must
+both include the Physical Hermes overlay; older peers do not implement this extension.
